Commit:     totalwindupflightsystems <totalwindupflightsystems@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Sun Oct 4 14:50:14 2026 -0500

    fix(s3): per-namespace deadline keeps `sync all` terminating. Addresses S3-ALERT-002.
    
    `s3 sync all push` ran each namespace with NO per-namespace bound, so one
    huge namespace pinned the whole pass: the `scheduler` namespace (210,692
    tracked files, ~46k-file delta after the 09-30 backup) outlived every
    3600s wrapper run — four consecutive "FAIL sync-all-deadline rc=124"
    (13:30/15:15/16:30/17:45Z) and a lock handed to stale-clear every ~2h15m
    since 10-04 05:45Z. Backup never advanced past 2026-09-30T12:46:44Z.
    
    Changes (src/s3/ + scripts/s3/ only; S3 protocol and bucket layout
    untouched):
    
    - syncNamespace takes opts.timeoutMs (default from S3_SYNC_ALL_DEADLINE_S,
      same env knob the wrapper uses for its whole-run timeout; 0 = legacy
      unbounded). Two layers bound a namespace:
      1. cooperative: push/pull loops poll the deadline BETWEEN file
         operations and abort cleanly, saving the manifest first so partial
         progress is durable (uploaded files skip on the next pass; files
         with no remote object re-upload regardless of manifest).
      2. backstop: a wall-clock Promise.race also bounds a stall INSIDE one
         operation (measured live: scheduler burned its window in the
         211-page listRemoteObjects phase, where no cooperative checkpoint
         exists; the raced branch drains idempotently in the background and
         releases the lock immediately).
    - syncAllNamespacesDetailed returns {stats, failures}; the legacy
      syncAllNamespaces wrapper keeps returning plain stats (src/s3/index.ts
      autopush path unchanged).
    - s3Sync reports every failed namespace BY NAME and sets exit code 1 —
      a pass that backed up nothing can never print "complete" + rc=0 again
      (the all-locks-held run of 09-30 did exactly that).
    - scripts/s3/duckbrain-s3-native-sync.sh synced from the DEPLOYED copy
      (the S3-GIT-007 deadline block existed only in ~/.hermes/scripts/;
      repo copy predated it).
    
    Verification (all live, 2026-10-04 ~18:40-18:55Z):
    - RED: sync-deadline-s3alert002.test.ts fails 8/11 on the pre-fix tree.
    - GREEN: new suite 11/11; full `npx vitest run` 201 files / 1621 tests,
      0 failures, rc=0; tsc --noEmit clean; prettier clean on touched files.
    - LIVE (prod config, real endpoint): S3_SYNC_ALL_DEADLINE_S=300 run
      TERMINATED in ~15 min with rc=1: "scheduler exceeded its 300s
      deadline (sync abandoned mid-flight)", then "push complete: 547
      namespaces, 24 files transferred", "1/548 namespace(s) failed this
      pass: FAILED scheduler". Lock released, pass continued past it.
    - The 18:45Z cron tick collided with the probe lock and failed LOUD
      and fast (rc=1 "lock held") instead of hanging.
    
    ch:trace row=S3-ALERT-002 evidence=/tmp/s3alert002-live-a.log + src/s3/sync-deadline-s3alert002.test.ts witness=live:sync-run
    
